                ("p", "A particulate filter needs heat and a spell of steady driving to regenerate. Many diesels in the south of Tenerife do short hops between urbanisations and never complete the cycle, so the filter gradually fills up. Sometimes an assisted regeneration at the workshop is enough; other times we need to find out why it's clogging: a dripping injector, a stuck EGR valve or a pressure sensor giving false readings. If we only treat the symptom, it will happen again."),
